<h1>sprite_get_height</h1>
<p>With this function you can find the height of the base sprite asset, with no transforms, in pixels.</p>
<p> </p>
<h4>Syntax:</h4>
<p class="code">sprite_get_height(index);</p>
<table>
<tbody>
<tr>
<th>Argument</th><th>Type</th>
<th>Description</th>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>index</td><td><span data-keyref="Type_Asset_Sprite"><a target="_blank" href="../../../../../The_Asset_Editors/Sprites.htm">Sprite Asset</a></span></td>
<td>The index of the sprite to find the height of.</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<p> </p>
<h4>Returns</h4>
<p class="code"><span data-keyref="Type_Real"><a target="_blank" href="../../../../GML_Overview/Data_Types.htm">Real</a></span></p>
<p> </p>
<h4>Example:</h4>
<p class="code">if (sprite_height != sprite_get_height(sprite_index)) <br/>
{<br/>
    image_yscale = 1;<br/>
}</p>
<p>The above code checks the height of the sprite as it is in the current instance and if there is a difference between that and the original base sprite, it resets the y axis scale.</p>
<p> </p>
<p> </p>
<p> </p>
